&lt;p&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://mui.com/material-ui/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Material UI&lt;/a&gt; is a comprehensive library of React components that features our independent implementation of Google&amp;rsquo;s &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://m2.material.io/design/introduction/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Material Design&lt;/a&gt; system.
It&amp;rsquo;s trusted by some of the world&amp;rsquo;s greatest product teams because it&amp;rsquo;s been rigorously battle-tested through more than a decade of development by thousands of open-source contributors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Material UI&amp;rsquo;s core functionality is extended by &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/mui/mui-x&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;MUI X&lt;/a&gt;, a suite of complex components for advanced use cases.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;documentation&#34;&gt;Documentation
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Get started in the &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://mui.com/material-ui/getting-started/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Material UI documentation&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;details&gt;
  &lt;summary&gt;Older versions&lt;/summary&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://v5.mui.com/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;v5.x&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://mui.com/material-ui/migration/upgrade-to-v6/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Upgrading from v5 to v6&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://v4.mui.com/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;v4.x&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://mui.com/material-ui/migration/migration-v4/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Upgrading from v4 to v5&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://v3.mui.com/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;v3.x&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://mui.com/material-ui/migration/migration-v3/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Upgrading from v3 to v4&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://v0.mui.com/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;v0.x&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://mui.com/material-ui/migration/migration-v0x/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Upgrading to v1&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/details&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;@next&lt;/code&gt; points to pre-releases.
Use &lt;code&gt;@latest&lt;/code&gt; for the latest stable release.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;joy-ui&#34;&gt;Joy UI
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;This repository also contains Joy UI, an experimental component library that implements our own in-house Joy Design.
Joy UI is in beta and &lt;em&gt;development is currently on hold&lt;/em&gt;.
When starting a new project from scratch, we recommend Material UI over Joy UI because we can guarantee ongoing support.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Keep in mind that the maintainers are primarily focused on other projects and may not be able to respond in a timely manner to issues or pull requests related to Joy UI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;View the &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://mui.com/joy-ui/getting-started/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Joy UI documentation&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
